+## The store file
+
+By default tally reads and writes `tally.json` in whatever directory you run it
+from. You can override this with `--store` if you want to keep expenses somewhere
+specific, or to maintain separate stores for different purposes:
+
+```
+tally --store ~/finances/2024.json add 12.50 food
+```
+
+The `--store` flag comes before the subcommand and works with all of them.
 
